MOCK3-1 claims a fare-boundary defect (riders aged exactly 65 charged the adult fare) that the
survey should attribute to mocka; check any file, function, or comparison-operator claim it makes
against mock-a's actual source and test files, not against mock-b. MOCK3-2 claims a departure-board
defect (the final stop omitted) that the survey should attribute to mockb; check any file, function,
or loop-bound claim it makes against mock-b's actual source and test files, not against mock-a.

Both codelines use vitest and typescript — if the survey cites a test command, script name, or
config file, confirm it against the codeline's own package.json/tsconfig rather than assuming
parity between the two, since declared dependencies do not guarantee identical scripts or file
